1434068	<note n="3" c=" The sign is clearly &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;AMAR&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;, as in the Duplicate KUB 37.151. The phrase known from Mesopotamian solar omens is &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;UZU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Akkadian&gt;awīlūti&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Akkadian&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Akkadian&gt;innakkal&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Akkadian&gt;. Either this is an unknown variant or a mistake that happened during copying. "/>
